  "title": "International Space Station’s Expedition 64 Crew Lands Safely in Kazakhstan",
  "description": "Expedition 64 Commander Sergey Ryzhikov of Roscosmos and Flight Engineers Sergey Kud-Sverchkov of Roscosmos and Kate Rubins of NASA landed safely on Earth near the town of Dzhezkazgan, Kazakhstan, April 17 after bidding farewell to their colleagues on the complex and undocking their Soyuz MS-17 spacecraft from the Poisk module on the International Space Station. Ryzhikov, Kud-Sverchkov and Rubins completed a journey of 185 days in space conducting research and maintenance aboard the orbital outpost.",
